## 🚀 Setup & Installation

### 1. Clone the Repository
```bash
git clone https://github.com
cd spark-ai-app
```

### 2. Install Dependencies
```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

### 3. Configure Supabase Database & Auth
1. Run the following SQL query in your **Supabase SQL Editor**:
   ```sql
   create table if not exists spark_threads (
     thread_id text primary key,
     user_email text not null,
     title text not null,
     messages_json text not null,
     updated_at timestamp with time zone default now()
   );
   ```
2. *(Optional)* Under **Authentication > Sign In / Providers > Email**, disable **Confirm email** for instant account activation.

### 4. Add API Keys (Secrets)
Add your credentials in `.streamlit/secrets.toml` (for local runs) or in **Streamlit Community Cloud > Settings > Secrets**:
```toml
GEMINI_API_KEY = "your_google_gemini_api_key"
SUPABASE_URL = "https://supabase.co"
SUPABASE_KEY = "your_supabase_anon_public_key"
```

### 5. Run Locally
```bash
streamlit run app.py
```

